  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array of integers, determine if it's possible to form at least one non-degenerate triangle using any three values from the array.\n\nA non-degenerate triangle has sides that satisfy these conditions:\n\n\nSum of any two sides must be greater than the third side\nEach side must have positive length\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - the number of test cases\nFor each test case:\n\nFirst line contains an integer NNN - the size of array\nSecond line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​ - the array elements\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, print a single line:\n\"YES\" if a valid triangle can be formed\n\"NO\" if no valid triangle can be formed",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "3≤N≤1033 \\leq N \\leq 10^33≤N≤103",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n5 3 4\n4\n1 12 10 30",
        "output": "YES\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1:\n\nUsing sides 3, 4, 5:\n3 + 4 > 5 \n4 + 5 > 3 \n5 + 3 > 4 \nTherefore, a valid triangle can be formed.\n\nTest Case 2:\n\nNo combination of three numbers can form a triangle.\nFor example, with 10, 12, 30: \n10 + 12 = 22, which is not > 30"
      }
    ]
  },
